Q: Correlation ID kya hoti hai?

Correlation ID (sometimes called Request ID) = ek unique ID jo ek request ke saath poori journey mein travel karti hai —
API Gateway → Service A → Service B → logs / queues — taake us request ke saare logs ek ID se search ho saken.

Example:
X-Correlation-Id: 8f7a91c2-4b21-4c9a-9e11-22aa33bb44cc

────────────────────────────────────────
Why needed?

Microservices mein ek user call kai services touch karti hai.
Bina common ID ke har service ke logs alag dikhte hain — failure trace karna mushkil.

With Correlation ID:
grep / Kibana search → 8f7a91c2
→ Gateway + Order + Payment + Notification sab logs mil jate hain.

────────────────────────────────────────
Correlation ID vs Trace ID

| Term            | Typical meaning                                      |
| --------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| Correlation ID  | App/business request id (often custom header)        |
| Trace ID        | Distributed tracing id (OpenTelemetry / Zipkin / Jaeger) |
| Span ID         | One hop/operation inside a trace                     |

Practice:
- Many teams use Trace ID as the correlation id in logs.
- Some keep both: business Correlation-Id + OpenTelemetry TraceId.

────────────────────────────────────────
How it flows

Client / Gateway generates ID (or accepts incoming)
        ↓
Header: X-Correlation-Id / X-Request-Id
        ↓
Service A logs it (MDC)
        ↓
Outbound HTTP / Kafka header mein same ID forward
        ↓
Service B logs same ID

Spring tip:
- Put id in MDC (Mapped Diagnostic Context) so every log line includes it
- Filter / interceptor at entry; clear MDC in finally

────────────────────────────────────────
Related question: Ek service call ke logs kaise trace karenge?

1. Take Correlation ID / Trace ID from failing response or gateway log
2. Search that ID in log aggregator (ELK / Loki / CloudWatch)
3. Or open distributed trace in Jaeger / Tempo / Zipkin
4. See which service/span failed or was slow

See also: "How would you trace a request across distributed services"

────────────────────────────────────────
✅ Interview one-liner

Correlation ID ek unique request identifier hai jo har service call aur log line ke saath propagate hoti hai,
taake distributed system mein ek request ka full path logs se trace ho sake.
